IMPORT prelude

-- National Parks Board Act 1996 (Singapore) -- the rules with decision content in an institutional Act: execution under seal
-- (s 4(2)), delegation and subdelegation (s 10), protection from personal liability (s 11), the financial year (s 19), the
-- symbol offence (s 29), the exclusion of liability for paid information (s 30), where moneys go (s 31), the Minister's approval
-- (s 32 and Second Schedule paras 15, 16), the constitution and proceedings of the Board (First Schedule paras 1, 9, 11, 13), and
-- the pension apportionment on the 1996 transfer of staff (Third Schedule para 3).
--
-- Edition: 2020 Revised Edition, informal consolidation, as deposited at ../../registers/source-bundle/NPBA1996.txt, incorporating
-- amendments up to and including 1 December 2021 (latest annotation seen: Act 10 of 2019).
--
-- WHY THIS ACT. Cited by 11 of the 527 Singapore Acts deposited in this repository. SCOPED to the provisions that decide something.
-- Not encoded: the list of functions (s 6) and powers (s 7, Second Schedule) beyond the two that need the Minister's approval,
-- Ministerial directions (s 8), staff appointment (s 12), grants, shares, bank accounts and investment (ss 14-17), estimates
-- (s 18), the 1996 transfer of property and agreements (ss 20-22), the 2019 transfer of the AVA veterinary undertaking (Part 7,
-- ss 23-28) and the rest of the Third Schedule.
--
-- NAIVE ENCODING. Straight from the deposited text with the writing-l4-rules skill. No pipeline, no coverage table,
-- no independent test pass, no human gate. See NOTES.md.

§ `National Parks Board Act 1996 -- the Board`

§§ `4(2) -- documents under the common seal`

-- s 4(2): "every document to which the common seal is affixed must be signed by any 2 members generally or specially authorised
-- by the Board for the purpose or by one member so authorised and the Chief Executive."
GIVEN `authorised members who signed` IS A NUMBER, `the Chief Executive signed` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the sealed document is properly signed` IF
        `authorised members who signed` >= 2
    OR  (`authorised members who signed` >= 1 AND `the Chief Executive signed`)

§§ `10 -- delegation and subdelegation`

-- s 10(1): the Board may delegate "any of its functions, duties or powers under this Act or any other Act" by resolution and
-- written notice to (a) a member; (b) the Chief Executive, any employee "or any other person performing duties in the Board";
-- (c) a committee appointed under s 9; (d) "a wholly-owned subsidiary company of the Board"; (e) "a person engaged as a
-- contractor by the Board".
-- s 10(3): (1) and (2) do not apply to (a) "the power to borrow money"; (b) the power to raise or grant loans or advances or
-- subscribe to stocks, shares, bonds or debentures; (c) a function, duty or power declared by an Act "to be non-delegable".
DECLARE Delegate IS ONE OF
    `a member of the Board`
    `the Chief Executive`
    `an employee of the Board`
    `a committee of the Board`
    `a wholly-owned subsidiary of the Board`
    `a contractor engaged by the Board`
    `an unconnected outside company`

DECLARE Power IS ONE OF
    `managing a public park`
    `an enforcement power under another Act`
    `the power to borrow money`
    `the power to subscribe to shares`
    `a power declared non-delegable`

GIVEN `the delegate` IS A Delegate
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is an eligible delegate` IF
    CONSIDER `the delegate`
    WHEN `an unconnected outside company` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

GIVEN `the power` IS A Power
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is delegable` IF
    CONSIDER `the power`
    WHEN `the power to borrow money` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `the power to subscribe to shares` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `a power declared non-delegable` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

GIVEN `the power` IS A Power, `the delegate` IS A Delegate, `by resolution and written notice` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Board may delegate it` IF
        `is delegable` `the power`
    AND `is an eligible delegate` `the delegate`
    AND `by resolution and written notice`

-- s 10(2): a delegation (a) to a person in (1)(a), (b) or (c) "may authorise the delegate to subdelegate ... to another member,
-- an appropriately qualified employee of the Board or person performing duties in the Board"; (b) to a person in (1)(d) or (e)
-- may authorise subdelegation "to an appropriately qualified employee of that delegate".
-- s 10(4): a subdelegate "is not authorised to further delegate that function, duty or power to anyone else."
DECLARE Recipient IS ONE OF
    `another member of the Board`
    `a qualified employee of the Board`
    `an unqualified employee of the Board`
    `a qualified employee of the delegate`
    `an outside person`

GIVEN `the delegate` IS A Delegate
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is an internal delegate` IF
    CONSIDER `the delegate`
    WHEN `a member of the Board` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `the Chief Executive` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `an employee of the Board` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a committee of the Board` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

GIVEN `the delegate` IS A Delegate
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is an external delegate` IF
    CONSIDER `the delegate`
    WHEN `a wholly-owned subsidiary of the Board` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a contractor engaged by the Board` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

GIVEN `the delegate` IS A Delegate, `the recipient` IS A Recipient
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is a permitted subdelegate` IF
        (`is an internal delegate` `the delegate`
         AND (    `the recipient` EQUALS `another member of the Board`
              OR  `the recipient` EQUALS `a qualified employee of the Board`))
    OR  (`is an external delegate` `the delegate`
         AND `the recipient` EQUALS `a qualified employee of the delegate`)

GIVEN `the delegate` IS A Delegate, `the recipient` IS A Recipient, `the delegation authorises subdelegation` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `the one delegating is itself a subdelegate` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the subdelegation is valid` IF
        `the delegation authorises subdelegation`
    AND (NOT `the one delegating is itself a subdelegate`)
    AND `is a permitted subdelegate` `the delegate` `the recipient`

§§ `11 -- protection from personal liability`

-- s 11: "No liability shall lie against any member, any committee member, the Chief Executive or any employee, delegate or
-- subdelegate of the Board, or any other person acting under the direction of the Board, for anything ... done or purported to
-- be done, or omitted to be done, in good faith and with reasonable care in" exercising a power or performing a function under
-- this Act.
GIVEN `a person covered by s 11` IS A BOOLEAN, `acting under this Act` IS A BOOLEAN, `in good faith` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `with reasonable care` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `personal liability is excluded` IF
    `a person covered by s 11` AND `acting under this Act` AND `in good faith` AND `with reasonable care`

§§ `19 -- financial year`

-- s 19: "The financial year of the Board begins on 1 April of each year and ends on 31 March of the succeeding year."
GIVEN `month` IS A NUMBER, `year` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the financial year starting in` MEANS
    IF `month` >= 4 THEN `year` ELSE `year` - 1

§§ `29 -- the Board's symbols`

-- s 29(2): "Any person who, without the permission of the Board, uses a symbol or representation identical with any of the
-- Board's symbols, or which so resembles any of the Board's symbols as to or be likely to deceive or cause confusion, shall be
-- guilty of an offence and shall be liable on conviction to a fine not exceeding $10,000 or to imprisonment for a term not
-- exceeding 6 months or to both."
GIVEN `uses the symbol` IS A BOOLEAN, `has the Board's permission` IS A BOOLEAN, `identical to a Board symbol` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `likely to deceive or confuse` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the symbol offence is committed` IF
        `uses the symbol`
    AND (NOT `has the Board's permission`)
    AND (`identical to a Board symbol` OR `likely to deceive or confuse`)

`the maximum fine for the symbol offence` MEANS 10000
`the maximum imprisonment in months for the symbol offence` MEANS 6

§§ `30 -- information supplied for a fee`

-- s 30: "Where the Board provides a service to the public whereby information is supplied to the public on payment of a
-- prescribed fee", neither the Board nor its employees are liable for loss "by reason of any error or omission ... if made in
-- good faith and in the ordinary course of the discharge of the duties of those employees."
-- Unlike s 11, no reasonable care is required. Information supplied free is outside s 30 (and s 11 does not name the Board
-- itself).
GIVEN `supplied on payment of a prescribed fee` IS A BOOLEAN, `in good faith` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `in the ordinary course of duties` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Board is not liable for the error` IF
    `supplied on payment of a prescribed fee` AND `in good faith` AND `in the ordinary course of duties`

§§ `31 -- where moneys go`

-- s 31(1): moneys recovered or sums collected under this Act or any other Act administered by the Board, "other than composition
-- sums", are paid into the general funds of the Board. (2): "All composition sums ... are to be paid into the Consolidated Fund."
DECLARE Money IS ONE OF
    `a composition sum`
    `a licence fee`
    `a park admission charge`
    `a sum recovered in a civil claim`

DECLARE Fund IS ONE OF
    `the Board's general funds`
    `the Consolidated Fund`

GIVEN `the money` IS A Money
GIVETH A Fund
`where the money goes` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the money`
    WHEN `a composition sum` THEN `the Consolidated Fund`
    OTHERWISE `the Board's general funds`

§§ `32 and Second Schedule paras 15, 16 -- what needs the Minister's approval`

-- Second Schedule para 15: "With the approval of the Minister, to join in the formation of a company, association, trust or
-- partnership or enter into a joint venture"; para 16: "With the approval of the Minister, to raise loans". s 32(1): the Board
-- may "with the approval of the Minister" make regulations. s 17: investment under "the standard investment power of statutory
-- bodies" (no approval stated). Para 19: "To charge fees" (no approval stated).
DECLARE Step IS ONE OF
    `raising a loan`
    `joining in forming a company`
    `entering a joint venture`
    `making regulations`
    `investing its moneys`
    `charging fees for its facilities`
    `appointing a committee`

GIVEN `the step` IS A Step
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `needs the Minister's approval` IF
    CONSIDER `the step`
    WHEN `raising a loan` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `joining in forming a company` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `entering a joint venture` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `making regulations` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

§§ `First Schedule -- constitution and proceedings`

-- Para 1: "a Chairperson; and (b) not less than 6 but not more than 10 other members".
GIVEN `number of other members` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Board's size is lawful` IF
    `number of other members` >= 6 AND `number of other members` <= 10

-- Para 9: office vacated if the member "(a) has been absent, without leave of the Board, from 3 consecutive meetings"; or (b)
-- becomes disqualified under para 11. Para 11: must not be appointed or continue if (a) "an undischarged bankrupt or has made any
-- arrangement with his or her creditors"; (b) "sentenced to imprisonment for a term of at least 6 months and has not received a
-- free pardon"; (c) "has a mental disorder and is incapable of managing himself or herself or his or her affairs".
-- No time limit is stated on (b): a sentence at any time counts.
DECLARE Member HAS
    `undischarged bankrupt` IS A BOOLEAN
    `has made an arrangement with creditors` IS A BOOLEAN
    `months of imprisonment sentenced` IS A NUMBER
    `received a free pardon` IS A BOOLEAN
    `has a mental disorder` IS A BOOLEAN
    `incapable of managing own affairs` IS A BOOLEAN
    `consecutive meetings missed without leave` IS A NUMBER

GIVEN `the member` IS A Member
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is disqualified` IF
        `the member`'s `undischarged bankrupt`
    OR  `the member`'s `has made an arrangement with creditors`
    OR  (`the member`'s `months of imprisonment sentenced` >= 6 AND (NOT `the member`'s `received a free pardon`))
    OR  (`the member`'s `has a mental disorder` AND `the member`'s `incapable of managing own affairs`)

GIVEN `the member` IS A Member
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the office is vacated` IF
        `the member`'s `consecutive meetings missed without leave` >= 3
    OR  `is disqualified` `the member`

-- Para 13(2): "At every meeting of the Board, 5 members form a quorum."
GIVEN `members present` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the meeting is quorate` IF
    `members present` >= 5

-- Para 13(3): "adopted by a simple majority of the members present and voting except that in the case of an equality of votes the
-- Chairperson or member presiding has a casting vote in addition to his or her original vote."
GIVEN `votes for` IS A NUMBER, `votes against` IS A NUMBER, `the casting vote is for` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the decision is adopted` IF
        `votes for` > `votes against`
    OR  (`votes for` = `votes against` AND `the casting vote is for`)

-- Para 13(6): "Where at least 4 members of the Board request the Chairperson by written notice signed by them to convene a meeting
-- ... the Chairperson must, within 7 days from the receipt of the notice, convene a meeting for that purpose."
GIVEN `members who signed the written request` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Chairperson must convene a meeting` IF
    `members who signed the written request` >= 4

`days to convene a requisitioned meeting` MEANS 7

§§ `Third Schedule para 3 -- pension apportionment on the 1996 transfer`

-- Para 3: for a person transferred under s 21, "the Government is liable to pay to the Board such portion of any gratuity, pension
-- or allowance payable to that person on his or her retirement as the same bears to the proportion which the aggregate amount of
-- his or her pensionable emoluments during his or her service with the Government bears to the aggregate amount of his or her
-- pensionable emoluments during his or her service under both the Government and the Board."
-- INFERENCE: the wording is tangled ("as the same bears to the proportion which"); it is read here as the Government's share being
-- the benefit times Government emoluments over total emoluments.
GIVEN `the benefit` IS A NUMBER, `emoluments under the Government` IS A NUMBER, `emoluments under the Board` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the Government's share of the benefit` MEANS
    `the benefit` * `emoluments under the Government` / (`emoluments under the Government` + `emoluments under the Board`)
